// title: Who approved which email remediation, now that Advanced Hunting carries it
// date: 2026-09-24
// product: Defender for Office 365
// tables: EmailPostDeliveryEvents
// purpose: MC1478005 adds an ApproverUpn column to EmailPostDeliveryEvents, GA worldwide and enabled by default. Approval was previously a click-through in Action Center, one action at a time. As a column it becomes a pattern you can look at: who approves, how much, and when.
// source: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/defender-xdr/advanced-hunting-emailpostdeliveryevents-table
// archived by tools/kql_archive.py (CLAUDE.md 5l)
// Microsoft SOC Brief - 24 September 2026
// MC1478005: EmailPostDeliveryEvents gains ApproverUpn, naming who approved a remediation.
// Table and columns: EmailPostDeliveryEvents -
// https://learn.microsoft.com/defender-xdr/advanced-hunting-emailpostdeliveryevents-table
// Run this first to confirm the column has reached this tenant: if ApproverUpn is not yet
// present the query fails on an unknown column rather than returning a wrong answer.
EmailPostDeliveryEvents
| where Timestamp > ago(30d)
| where isnotempty(ApproverUpn)
| summarize Approvals = count(),
            Actions   = make_set(ActionType, 20),
            FirstSeen = min(Timestamp),
            LastSeen  = max(Timestamp)
        by ApproverUpn
| order by Approvals desc
